e,v=ev(69,'30–39','Continue with lamp, modaka/apūpa/laḍḍū/pāyasa with sugar and ghee-cooked food, coconut/grapes/mango/pomegranate, areca/cardamom/clove/betel leaves, gold dakṣiṇā, and twenty-one dūrvā with a twenty-one-name list. Offer camphor light and campaka/aśoka/bakula/pārijāta flower handfuls. The hymn attributes creation, protection, destruction and universal appearance to the elephant-faced deity; the bowing formula praises obstacle-removal, devotee relief, liberation, knowledge and Vedic foundation. Parenthetical Vedic alternatives include Puruṣa-body social and cosmic emanations.',[('Brahmā',D),(KF,F),('Gaṇeśa',D),('Dūrvā',C),('Puruṣasūkta ritual alternatives in69',T),('Puruṣa in69 ritual alternative',C),(RIT,'FAMILY')],story=S4,outcome='Offerings, names and cosmic praise remain explicitly within prescribed recitation.')
