e,v=ev(69,'40–50','After the hymn bow repeatedly and make twenty-one circumambulations according to ability. The prayer says those seeking tasks without worship of Gaṇeśa are ruined. Offer vāyana to the Brahmin teacher and special arghya with fruit, flowers, rice, water and dakṣiṇā. Invoke Heramba for distress-removal and honour Indra and the surrounding world guardians. Prepare ghee-cooked modakas with cooked mung and sesame and other foods/betel as able, then offer twenty-one dūrvā separately using the verse names. This second sequence includes Abhayaprada, Amareśvara, Gajavakra and Sarvavidyāpradāyaka alongside names shared with the earlier list; the distinct printed forms are retained.',[('Brahmā',D),(KF,F),('Gaṇeśa',D),('Indra',D),('World guardians in69','FAMILY'),('Sankaṣṭa ritual teacher','SAGE'),('Dūrvā',C),(RIT,'FAMILY')],story=S4,outcome='Circumambulation, teacher offering, guardian worship and separate sprout-name sequence extend the prescribed services.')
