e,v=ev(69,'51–62','Request satisfaction with the properly directed worship, fulfillment of inner wishes, removal of obstacles and present enemies, destruction of enemies’ intelligence and prosperity of friends. Bow repeatedly and perform one hundred eight homa offerings. For vow-completion prepare vāyana of modakas or laḍḍū/vaṭaka and other foods with twenty-one fruits, wrap in red cloth and give to the teacher. Hear the sacred story and offer arghya to the tithi, then Gaṇeśa, then Moon seven times. The Moon formula calls him milk-ocean-born, arising in Atri’s lineage, accompanied by Rohiṇī. Ask the deity’s pardon, feed Brahmins, eat their offered remainder silently in seven mouthfuls according to ability and comfort, and perform this procedure in all four months.',[('Brahmā',D),(KF,F),('Gaṇeśa',D),('Moon',D),('Atri',S),('Rohiṇī',D),('Sankaṣṭa caturthī tithi',D),('Sankaṣṭa ritual teacher','SAGE'),('Sankaṣṭa fed Brahmins','FAMILY'),(RIT,'FAMILY')],story=S4,outcome='The detailed worship chapter ends with monthly repetition; the broader explanation and udyāpana continue.')
