e,v=ev(69,'17–37','The parenthetical ritual alternatives recite Puruṣa as thousand-headed, thousand-eyed and thousand-footed, embracing what has been and will be; Virāj arises, and Puruṣa arises from Virāj. Gods perform sacrifice with Puruṣa as offering, spring as ghee, summer as fuel and autumn as offering-material; gods, Sādhyas and sages worship the primordial sacrificial Puruṣa. From the sacrifice arise the curd-ghee mixture and aerial, forest and village animals, Ṛc/Sāman/metres/Yajus, horses, creatures with teeth on both sides, cattle, goats and sheep. The bodily social formula assigns mouth to Brahmins, arms to Rājanyas, thighs to Vaiśyas and feet to Śūdras. The cosmic formula gives Moon from mind, Sun from eye, wind/breath from ear, Fire from mouth, interspace from navel, heaven from head, earth from feet and directions from ears. The gods bind Puruṣa as sacrificial animal with seven enclosures and twenty-one fuel-sticks; the closing alternative praises ancient Sādhyas in heaven. These are prescribed Vedic recitations, without a new narrated Gaṇeśa birth or universal biological identity assertion.',[('Puruṣasūkta ritual alternatives in69',T),('Puruṣa in69 ritual alternative',C),('Virāj in69 ritual alternative',C),('Gods',C),('Sādhyas in69 ritual alternative',C),('Sages',C),('Vasanta in69 sacrificial formula',C),('Grīṣma in69 sacrificial formula',C),('Śarad in69 sacrificial formula',C),('Moon',D),('Sun',D),('Wind in69 ritual alternative',D),('Fire',D),('Puruṣa formula Brahmins',C),('Puruṣa formula Rājanyas',C),('Puruṣa formula Vaiśyas',C),('Puruṣa formula Śūdras',C),('Heaven in69 ritual alternative',L),('Earth in69 ritual alternative',L),('Interspace in69 ritual alternative',L)],story=S4,outcome='All named cosmogonic formula roles remain source-attributed ritual assertions.')
val('Puruṣasūkta ritual alternatives in69','ritual_social_body_mapping','Brahmins mouth; Rājanyas arms; Vaiśyas thighs; Śūdras feet in69.30 alternative.',e)
