e,v=ev(70,'13–15','Brahmā says Pradyumna practices the pleasing vow and hears from Nārada that the son is detained in Bāṇāsura’s city. At Uddhava’s instruction Kṛṣṇa, fearing a battle with Īśvara, properly practices the vow once. He goes to Śoṇitapura, defeats Bāṇāsura in combat, and quickly brings Aniruddha with Uṣā.',[('Brahmā',D),('Pradyumna',F),('Nārada',S),('Uddhava',F),('Kṛṣṇa',D),('Śiva',D),('Bāṇāsura',A),('Śoṇitapura',L),('Aniruddha',F),('Uṣā',F),('Citralekhā',F)],story=S5,outcome='Nārada locates the detained son; one vow, actual combat victory and retrieval follow. No weapons or marriage ceremony are supplied here.')
