e,v=ev(70,'16–25','Brahmā says he too performed the vow desiring creation and produced varied creation through its power. Gods, asuras, humans, sages, Dānavas, Yakṣas, Kinnaras, Uragas and Rākṣasas also practiced to quell obstacles. He instructs practice during distress, hearing the story, silent eating with hands between knees while meditating Gaṇeśa, and sharing the Brahmins’ remainder with relatives. Tasks accomplish in few months. Teach neither non-devotees, atheists nor deceitful people, but a son, pupil or virtuous devotee. Calling the king dear, righteous and a worker for public good, Brahmā says to perform this before other vows; men and women should perform it before intended tasks.',[('Brahmā',D),(KF,F),('Gaṇeśa',D),('Gods',C),('Asuras',C),('Humans',C),('Sages',C),('Dānavas',C),('Yakṣas',C),('Kinnaras',C),('Uragas',C),('Rākṣasas',C),(RIT,'FAMILY')],story=S5,outcome='Reported creation and wider practitioners support instructions, timing and transmission restrictions.')
power('Brahmā',e,v,motive='Create.',mechanism='Varied creation is produced through the vow’s power.',trigger='His actual past performance of the vow.',notes='Brahmā’s attributed retrospective account70.16, not a new personal appearance/grant dialogue.')
power(RIT,e,v,mechanism='Obstacle-relief and desired task accomplishment in few months.',trigger='Practice the vow during distress or before intended tasks.',restrictions='Do not teach non-devotees, atheists or deceitful people; give instruction to son, pupil or virtuous devotee. Perform before other vows as prescribed.',duration='Few months, without an exact number.')
e,v=ev(70,'26','Sūta says the king hears and properly performs the vow for relief from all distress. Its power enables him to conquer enemies and enjoy an untroubled kingdom with sons. This closing statement reports the royal outcome concisely; the witness proceeds to a further completion procedure and fuller sonbirth account, so it is not treated as exhaustive closure of the larger Kṛtavīrya family history.',[('Sūta',S),(KV,F),('Unnamed sons in70 closing statement','FAMILY')],story=S3,outcome='A source closing outcome is recorded separately from the following fuller family account.')
power(KV,e,v,mechanism='Conquers enemies and enjoys a kingdom without trouble with sons.',trigger='Properly performs the vow to relieve distress.',notes='Sūta’s concise chapter70 closing report; not a reconstruction of every son’s later chronology.')
S6=S4
e,v=ev(71,'1–9','The king asks Brahmā to explain udyāpana for public benefit. Brahmā prescribes vow-completion in the first, fifth or seventh month. Make a flower pavilion decorated with various fabrics and a multicoloured sarvatobhadra arrangement; worship on a kalaśa as before with sandal and flowers. Give coconut arghya to the tithi, Gaṇeśa and Moon. Their formulas ask distress-removal; the Moon formula again gives milk-ocean and Atri-lineage origin and Rohiṇī accompaniment. Offer edible, chewable, lickable, drinkable and suckable foods and many fruits.',[(KF,F),('Brahmā',D),('Gaṇeśa',D),('Moon',D),('Atri',S),('Rohiṇī',D),('Sankaṣṭa caturthī tithi',D),(RIT,'FAMILY')],story=S6,outcome='Exact alternative completion months and separate recipient sequence are prescribed.')
e,v=ev(71,'10–17','Choose a teacher and twenty-one officiants. Perform ten thousand homa offerings with Gaṇānāṃ tvā, or use the root mantra for one thousand, half that, or one hundred eight offerings; then give bali, full offering and vasordhārā. Finish homa and feed Brahmins. Give paired garments, kalaśas, dakṣiṇā and seats according to capacity without deceit about means. Honour the fed teacher with clothes/ornaments and give fruit-vāyana, a winnowing basket filled with pāyasa wrapped in red cloth, the gold Gaṇeśa image with dakṣiṇā, an āḍhaka of sesame, and an adorned kapilā cow with calf. Request the Brahmins’ pardon, praying Vighneśa be pleased. Completing udyāpana gives horse-sacrifice merit.',[(KF,F),('Brahmā',D),('Sankaṣṭa ritual teacher','SAGE'),('Twenty-one Sankaṣṭa officiants','FAMILY'),('Sankaṣṭa fed Brahmins','FAMILY'),('Gaṇeśa',D),('Gaṇānāṃ tvā mantra',T),('Gaṇeśa root mantra in71',T),('Kapilā cow and calf gift in71',C),(RIT,'FAMILY')],story=S6,outcome='Completion protocol reaches its stated merit and closing pardon request.')
power(RIT,e,v,mechanism='Horse-sacrifice merit.',trigger='Perform the prescribed vow udyāpana.',notes='Prescribed result, not an actual horse sacrifice or personal boon scene; exact alternative homa counts preserved in the event.')
e,v=ev(71,'18–25','Kṛtavīrya’s father says Brahmā gave him these instructions for public benefit and tells his son to practice carefully for offspring. Indra says the intelligent performer follows every paternal instruction; verse19 names him Kārtavīrya, retaining the same name issue flagged in68. Learned scholars explain the vow. A gold image with Siddhi and Buddhi is installed in a great pavilion amid Brahmin recitation, Purāṇa learning, singing, dance, heavenly-reaching instrument sounds and some debate with mediators. The king japs, offers homa, worships and feeds many Brahmins. Adorned himself, he gives ten thousand cows to adorned Brahmins, food and many gifts to poor, blind and destitute people, then receives the truthful ascetic Brahmins’ blessings for a son.',[(KF,F),(KV,F),('Indra',D),('Brahmā',D),('Kṛtavīrya interpreting scholars','FAMILY'),('Gaṇeśa',D),('Siddhi (dakṣiṇā maiden)',F),('Buddhi (dakṣiṇā maiden)',F),('Kṛtavīrya assembled public','FAMILY'),('Sankaṣṭa fed Brahmins','FAMILY'),('Royal vow pavilion in71',L),('Poor recipients of royal gifts in71','FAMILY')],story=S3,outcome='Actual observance, ten-thousand-cow giving and requested son-blessings follow; gold image companions are not a new marriage narrative.')
e,v=ev(71,'26–29','Through the Brahmins’ blessings the royal wife becomes pregnant within a short time and gives birth at an auspicious moment to a son with marks. Delighted, the king gives many gifts, later performs the son’s vratabandha and marriage, and consecrates the knowledgeable son in the realm. Enjoying a good son and pleasures, he reaches the Lord’s state at the end. All officiants, scholars and onlookers reach Gaṇeśa’s abode through his merit. This is the chapter’s concise outcome; chapter72 begins a fuller account of that son and is not yet extracted.',[(KV,F),('Sugandhā (Kṛtavīrya wife)',F),('Unnamed son in71 concise outcome',F),('Twenty-one Sankaṣṭa officiants','FAMILY'),('Kṛtavīrya interpreting scholars','FAMILY'),('Royal vow onlookers in71','FAMILY'),('Gaṇeśa',D)],story=S3,outcome='Pregnancy, actual birth, later rites, succession and collective abode are reported. Exact royal actor variation and detailed72 chronology remain open.')
